  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **The World Is A Ghetto**: rare: 14 archived performances [3]\n- **Big Brother**: rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Use Me**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Chameleon, Drums [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2000-02-20.schoeps.ccm4** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 136 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The reviewer lived about a five-minute walk from The Stone Church at the time and believes they attended this show [2]\n- Microphones sat on a 4-foot stand onstage; the notes list Neal Evans on Hammond B3 organ [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2000-02-20.schoeps.ccm4**: taped by Paul deLima; transferred by Paul deLima; source: Schoeps CCM4 > Grace Design Lunatec V2 > Tascam DA-P1 @ 16bit 44.1kHz [1]. Also: Recorded with Schoeps CCM4 mics in ORTF through a Grace Design Lunatec V2 into a Tascam DA-P1 DAT at 16/44.1; Taped and transferred by Paul deLima; DAT went via HHb-850 to CD-R, then EAC, Sound Forge restoration (clipped peaks, fades), and FLAC [1]",
